{'sentiment score': 0, 'confidence': 0, 'reason': 'Fresh start adjustments to other noncurrent assets are recorded as an increase or decrease in the balance of total other noncurrent assets, which is reported as a debit to equity (additional paid-in capital) and/or net income. The fresh start adjustment is calculated by applying the replacement ratio from the acquisition agreement to the total amount of intangible assets acquired. Total other noncurrent assets include intangible assets with finite useful lives, identifiable intangible assets that are part of an arrangement that provides a benefit over more than one period, deferred tax assets resulting from temporary differences, and other noncurrent assets (such as property, plant, and equipment). The net income component of fresh start adjustments represents the increase in equity due to acquisition accounting. The additional paid-in capital component represents the purchase price allocated to the replacement ratio. Net income represents the amount of net income that is attributable to the replacement ratio over the remaining period for which the asset can be used.', 'company_name': 'COMPANY CONFORMED NAME:\t\t\tLonestar Resources US Inc.'}